        rules: {
          objective: 'Have your card survive while others fall (are matched).',
          gameplay: "Players buy a case card from the dealer; the dealer also takes a card. Cards are then revealed one by one from the shoe. When a revealed card matches a player's card (same rank), that player is eliminated. The last card remaining wins unless all bets are resolved earlier. Side bets are common.",
          keyRules: [
            'Each player buys one case card from the dealer; the dealer takes one.',
            'Cards are revealed one by one from the shoe (skinning).',
            "When a revealed card matches your card's rank, you are eliminated.",
            'The last card standing (The Skin) wins unless all bets are resolved earlier.',
            'Side bets between players are common.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Pure luck. There is no strategy in card selection since it's random. The strategy is in money management and reading opponents for side bets. If you see two 7s already gone, betting heavily on a 7 is safer (only one 7 left means less chance of falling soon? No, wait. If 2 7s are gone, there are 2 left in deck. Probability of falling is lower than if 3 were left? Yes. But eventually it must fall if you play to end of deck).",
          intermediate: "The 'Turn': Watch the turn cards. If a card hasn't appeared for a long time (is 'sleeping'), it's due. Gambler's fallacy, but common in Skin logic.",
          advanced: "Bankroll Management: In a fair game, variance will kill you. Don't bet everything on one card. Spread bets across multiple cards if allowed (playing two hands).",
          tips: [
            "Cheating (stacking the deck) was commonâ€”watch the dealer's hands.",
            "A 'Piky' deck is a rigged deck.",
